  "content": {
    "id": "p60-q24-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "24",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=x^2(2x-1)^4$ at $(1,1)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$10x-y-9=0$",
      "worked": "Using the product and chain rules:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=2x(2x-1)^4+8x^2(2x-1)^3\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=2x(2x-1)^3(6x-1).\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=2(1)(2-1)^3(6-1)\\\\m&=10.\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangent passes through $(1,1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=10(x-1)\\\\y&=10x-9\\\\10x-y-9&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 33
  },
